{#
  wastewater.j2
  =============
  Narrative text for the Wastewater treatment driver.

  Context variables (from _build_wastewater_ctx):
    is_point_mode             bool   True when treatment plants are modelled individually
    sewage_treated            metric – share of sewage treated (pp change)
    fecal_sludge              metric – share of fecal sludge treated (pp change)
    facility_count            metric – number of treatment plants (relative_pct change)
    treatment_level_changed   bool   – any significant shift in treatment level mix
    advanced_treatment_increased bool
    primary_treatment_increased  bool
#}
{% if sewage_treated.is_significant %}
The share of sewage receiving treatment {{ "increases" if sewage_treated.increased else "decreases" }} {{ sewage_treated.magnitude }} by {{ sewage_treated.abs_delta | num }} pp to {{ sewage_treated.scen_val }},
{{ "removing a larger share of pathogens before treated effluent reaches surface water" if sewage_treated.increased else "allowing more untreated pathogen loads to be discharged to surface water" }}.
{% endif %}
{% if fecal_sludge.is_significant %}
Fecal sludge treatment {{ "increases" if fecal_sludge.increased else "decreases" }} {{ fecal_sludge.magnitude }} by {{ fecal_sludge.abs_delta | num }} pp to {{ fecal_sludge.scen_val }}.
{% endif %}
{% if is_point_mode %}
{% if facility_count.is_significant %}
The number of wastewater treatment plants {{ "increases" if facility_count.increased else "decreases" }} by {{ facility_count.abs_delta | num }}% to {{ facility_count.scen_val }} facilities.
{% endif %}
{% if treatment_level_changed %}
{% if advanced_treatment_increased %}
The treatment capacity mix shifts towards tertiary and advanced treatment, improving pathogen removal efficiency.
{% elif primary_treatment_increased %}
A larger share of treatment capacity operates at primary level, which provides limited pathogen removal.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
